Q1 is answered and nothing was broken: a Ctrl-C at the REPL still prints the interrupt note and returns to a working prompt. I closed #988, since all three of its questions now have answers.

What I checked. I ran the built binary in a pty against a small fake OpenAI-compatible server and pressed Ctrl-C at two moments:
• (a) While waiting for the model's first token: it printed (interrupted — press Ctrl+C again to exit), showed a fresh prompt, answered the next prompt (PONG_SECOND_TURN), and /quit exited with code 0.
• (b) While the model's `bash sleep 30` was running: same result. The next request sent to the server had every tool call matched with its result, and no sleep process was left running.

Test added in src/prompt/cancel_mid_tool_tests.rs, the only file changed (commit f9d96bc9). It uses a fake provider that hangs until the run is cancelled, cancels it, and passes the real end-of-run messages to the same function the event loops use (handle_agent_end). That function must report a normal finished turn, with no error and no retry. As a contrast case, the same messages relabelled as an error must not count as a normal finish.
• I checked that the test can fail: removing Aborted from the "ignore" branch of the stop-reason classifier turns it red with ("FatalError", Some("Cancelled")). That is exactly the failure Q1 asked about. I put the line back and it passed again.
• Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the format check all pass.

One thing I didn't expect: a cancel during a tool call leaves no Aborted message at all, only a [Agent stopped: cancelled] note in the history. So my first version of the test was checking a case that can't happen. The test's own sanity check failed, and I switched it to cancelling while the model is still responding.

The other two questions: Q2 is null, because yoyo registers no on_error callback (grep -rn '\bon_error\b' src finds nothing). Q3 was a real bug, already fixed in 6b93f2e9. The closing comment on #988 has the raw transcripts for both cases.

Two separate bugs I filed instead of fixing here:
• #1061: when you Ctrl-C a tool, the model is told "💡 Recovery hint: The shell command failed. Check if the command exists…", and the cancel counts as a failure for that tool. This is the same mistake as Q3 (treating a cancel as a failure), but in what the model is told.
• #1062: passing --api-key on the command line doesn't skip the first-run setup wizard, and pressing Enter there falls back to Anthropic. Only a key in the environment or a config file is noticed. That's why the probe set OPENAI_API_KEY instead of using the flag.
